␛[1mfalco_misplaced_list                      ␛[0mA list is used where its expansion breaks the condition:
                                          as a macro, or as a single value; a list belongs inside a
                                          value list, `in (name)`.
␛[1mfalco_newer_syntax                        ␛[0mSyntax that only recent libsinsp releases parse (operator
                                          modifiers, `join`, `concat`, `getopt`, transformer
                                          arguments); an older Falco or Sysdig agent refuses the
                                          rule.
␛[1mfalco_no_evttype                          ␛[0mThe rule cannot be narrowed to a few event types
                                          (`evt.type`), so it runs on every event; Falco and Sysdig
                                          warn about the performance penalty.
␛[1mfalco_operator_type                       ␛[0mThe operator does not apply to the field's type (libsinsp
                                          `flt_is_comparable`); Falco refuses to load the rule.
␛[1mfalco_output_syntax                       ␛[0mThe output template does not format: a `%` at the end, a
                                          length with no field, or a token that is no field or
                                          transformer.
␛[1mfalco_parse_error                         ␛[0mThe Falco condition does not parse.
␛[1mfalco_regex_simple                        ␛[0mA `regex` check a plain operator (`=`, `contains`,
                                          `startswith`, `endswith`) could make, which libsinsp warns
                                          about: regex is the slowest check.
␛[1mfalco_rhs_field                           ␛[0mA field cannot be compared with another field here
                                          (`val(...)` or a transformer on the right): not with
                                          `pmatch` or `regex`, not on networks, not on fields that
                                          refuse it, and only between fields of the same type.
␛[1mfalco_transformer                         ␛[0mA field transformer cannot apply here: the field's type, a
                                          field that refuses transformers, or the arguments of
                                          `join`, `concat`, or `getopt`.
␛[1mfalco_transformer_as_value                ␛[0mA constant value that looks like a transformer call,
                                          compared as text.
␛[1mfalco_unknown_event                       ␛[0mThe event type is not in the driver's event table nor a
                                          syscall name; libsinsp refuses it.
␛[1mfalco_unknown_field                       ␛[0mThe field is not one Falco or its plugins define for the
                                          rule's event source; a plugin the engine does not know may
                                          add it.
␛[1mfalco_unknown_list                        ␛[0mThe name after a list operator, without parentheses, is
                                          not a list of the block or of the Falco default rules, so
                                          it is compared as a single value.
␛[1mfalco_unknown_macro                       ␛[0mThe name is not a macro of the block or of the Falco
                                          default rules; the tenant may define it, as Sysdig does
                                          for its managed macros.
␛[1mfalco_unknown_rule                        ␛[0mA tuning (`append_to_rule`) names a rule the Falco default
                                          rules do not define: Falco refuses the append, and on
                                          Sysdig the tenant must have that rule.
␛[1mfalco_unknown_source                      ␛[0mThe event source is not one Falco or its published plugins
                                          define, so its fields are not checked.
␛[1mfalco_unsafe_na_check                     ␛[0mA `ka.` or `jevt.` field compared with `<NA>`, which Falco
