␛[1mspl_dataset_not_declared                  ␛[0mThe sourcetype is not one the workspace declares in
                                          visibility.toml.
␛[1mspl_empty_command                         ␛[0mA command with no arguments: Splunk runs it, but it does
                                          nothing, returns no results, or fails at run time.
␛[1mspl_empty_stage                           ␛[0mA trailing | with no command; Splunk ignores it.
␛[1mspl_leading_not                           ␛[0mA base search that starts with NOT scans every event
                                          before excluding any.
␛[1mspl_parse_error                           ␛[0mThe SPL search does not parse.
␛[1mspl_search_operator                       ␛[0mA search clause compares with an operator search does not
                                          have (`==`, `<>`, `=>`, `=<`, `!~`): Splunk accepts it but
                                          the comparison never matches, or `=~`, which compares with
                                          a value that starts with `~`.
␛[1mspl_subsearch_truncation                  ␛[0mA subsearch is silently truncated at its result or time
                                          limit.
␛[1mspl_unknown_command                       ␛[0mThe SPL command is not in the Splunk Search Reference or a
                                          catalogued app such as MLTK: a warning, since an app on
                                          the search head can add commands, or an error when the
                                          name is one edit from a known command.
␛[1mspl_unknown_datamodel                     ␛[0mThe CIM data model or dataset is not one Splunk CIM
                                          defines.
␛[1mspl_unknown_datamodel_field               ␛[0mThe field is not in the CIM data model the search reads.
␛[1mspl_wildcard                              ␛[0mA leading or mid-token wildcard in a base search that
                                          nothing else narrows (no index, sourcetype, source, host,
                                          TERM() or macro) cannot use the index and scans every
                                          event.
␛[1msysdig_definition_duplicate               ␛[0mA name is defined more than once across the block's macros
                                          and lists.
␛[1msysdig_definition_name                    ␛[0mA block macro or list name is not
                                          `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`, or is a Falco operator or
                                          keyword.
␛[1msysdig_definition_order                   ␛[0mA block macro uses itself or a macro defined after it:
                                          Falco gives a macro no view of itself or later macros, and
                                          refuses it as an undefined macro.
␛[1msysdig_exception_shape                    ␛[0mAn exception's fields, comps, and values do not have a
                                          shape Falco's rule loader accepts
                                          (`validate_exception_info`).
␛[1msysdig_list_in_value                      ␛[0mA block list name appears in an exception value where
                                          Falco's expansion would not produce a value list.
␛[1msysdig_list_self_reference                ␛[0mA block list names itself as one of its items, so its own
                                          name stays in the expanded condition.
␛[1msysdig_priority                           ␛[0m`priority` is not one of Falco's eight priorities (or
                                          `INFO`), compared case-insensitively.
␛[1msysdig_rule_shape                         ␛[0mA Sysdig block is a new rule with a non-blank `condition`,
                                          or a tuning (`append_to_rule`) that appends a condition,
                                          exceptions, or both.
␛[1msysdig_source                             ␛[0m`source` is not an event source name (`[a-z][a-z0-9_]*`).
␛[1msysdig_tuning_keys                        ␛[0mA tuning (`append_to_rule`) inherits `output`, `priority`,
                                          `policies`, `source`, and `name` from the rule it tunes,
                                          so it must not set them.
␛[1mtechnique_not_enterprise                  ␛[0mThe ATT&CK technique is not in the Enterprise matrix that
                                          Elastic maps.
␛[1mtemplate_missing                          ␛[0m`opentide new` found no generated template or schema for
                                          the object type it was asked for.
␛[1mtemplates_fresh                           ␛[0mEvery template this opentide version generates exists and
                                          matches what it would write.
␛[1mthreshold_lookback                        ␛[0mA threshold rule's lookback exceeds its interval, so
                                          windows overlap and alerts repeat.
␛[1munknown_connector                         ␛[0m`sharing.toml` has a top-level array that names a sharing
                                          connector opentide does not have; it was skipped.
␛[1munknown_key                               ␛[0mA configuration file has a key opentide does not read,
                                          usually a misspelling.
␛[1murl_invalid                               ␛[0mA `sharing.toml` block's `url` is not an http(s) URL.
␛[1musage_error                               ␛[0mThe command line cannot be used as written, for a reason
                                          no other usage code covers.
␛[1musage_invalid_choice                      ␛[0mAn option or argument has a value outside the ones it
                                          accepts.
␛[1musage_invalid_value                       ␛[0mAn option has a value that cannot be used, although it is
                                          spelled correctly.
␛[1musage_missing_option                      ␛[0mA required option or argument is missing.
␛[1musage_needs_input                         ␛[0mThe command would ask a question, but nobody can answer
                                          it.
␛[1musage_tui_needs_tty                       ␛[0m`opentide tui` ran where it cannot draw: it needs a person
                                          at a terminal.
␛[1musage_unknown_command                     ␛[0mThe command line names a command that does not exist.
␛[1musage_unknown_option                      ␛[0mThe command line passes an option the command does not
                                          take.
␛[1musage_watch_needs_tty                     ␛[0m`validate --watch` ran where nobody can watch it.
␛[1mvocab_unknown                             ␛[0mA value is not in the vocabulary its field uses.
␛[1mvscode_settings                           ␛[0mThe workspace recommends the opentide VS Code extension
                                          (`opentidehq.opentide`) in `.vscode/extensions.json`, and
                                          `.vscode/settings.json` maps no object files to opentide's
                                          JSON schemas in `yaml.schemas`.
␛[1mvscode_snippets                           ␛[0mThe editor snippet file `opentide generate snippets`
                                          writes exists.
␛[1mworkspace                                 ␛[0mWhere the workspace is, and how it was found.
␛[1mworkspace_not_found                       ␛[0m`opentide new` ran outside a workspace: neither
                                          `.opentide/` nor `objects/` is there. Or the MCP server
                                          was started in an Agent Plugin's directory, which is not a
                                          workspace, and nothing named one.
␛[1myaml_parse                                ␛[0mAn object file is not valid YAML, or not one mapping, so
                                          it could not be loaded.
␛[1myara_duplicate_rule                       ␛[0mTwo YARA rules in one signature have the same name.
␛[1myara_duplicate_string                     ␛[0mTwo strings of one YARA rule have the same identifier.
␛[1myara_duplicate_tag                        ␛[0mA YARA rule repeats a tag.
␛[1myara_empty_signature                      ␛[0mThe YARA signature has no rule, or only private or global
                                          rules.
␛[1myara_entrypoint_deprecated                ␛[0mentrypoint is deprecated in libyara and refused by YARA-X;
                                          use pe.entry_point or elf.entry_point.
␛[1myara_hex_string                           ␛[0mA YARA hex string is invalid: an odd number of nibbles, a
                                          bad jump, or unbalanced alternatives.
␛[1myara_include                              ␛[0mA YARA signature uses an include directive, which no
                                          platform resolves: each API takes one text with no file
                                          system behind it.
␛[1myara_meta_missing                         ␛[0mA HarfangLab YARA rule has no meta `context`, which the
                                          HarfangLab profile recommends on every rule that is not
                                          private.
␛[1myara_module_not_imported                  ␛[0mA YARA module field or function is used without importing
                                          its module.
␛[1myara_module_unconfirmed                   ␛[0mThe YARA module is known but not confirmed on the
                                          platform's agents.
␛[1myara_number_out_of_range                  ␛[0mA YARA integer, size suffix, jump bound or string index is
                                          outside the range libyara accepts.
␛[1myara_parse_error                          ␛[0mThe YARA signature does not parse as libyara 4.5 reads it.
␛[1myara_regexp                               ␛[0mA YARA regular expression is invalid.
␛[1myara_rule_identifier_conflict             ␛[0mA YARA rule is named like a keyword, or matches a rule
                                          wildcard an earlier condition uses; a rule named like an
                                          imported module is yara_x_incompatible.
␛[1myara_signature_alias                      ␛[0mA `yara.signature` is a YAML alias of text anchored
                                          elsewhere in the file instead of YARA written in the
                                          block.
␛[1myara_slow_pattern                         ␛[0mlibyara warns that this YARA string or loop may slow
                                          scanning down.
␛[1myara_string_modifier                      ␛[0mlibyara refuses this combination of YARA string modifiers,
                                          or an xor or base64 argument is out of range.
␛[1myara_suspicious_expression                ␛[0mA YARA condition is invariant, unsatisfiable or not
                                          boolean, or compares an integer with a boolean.
␛[1myara_type                                 ␛[0mA YARA operator or function is applied to a value of the
                                          wrong type.
␛[1myara_undefined_identifier                 ␛[0mA YARA identifier is neither a rule defined earlier in the
                                          signature nor an imported module, or is used as libyara
                                          refuses: a module field called as a function, a module
                                          function named without a call, or a loop variable a loop
                                          already binds.
␛[1myara_undefined_string                     ␛[0mA YARA condition names a string ($id, #id, @id, !id or
                                          $prefix*) that the rule does not define.
␛[1myara_unknown_module                       ␛[0mA YARA import names a module libyara does not ship.
␛[1myara_unknown_module_member                ␛[0mThe YARA module has no such field or function, or the
                                          function takes other arguments.
␛[1myara_unreferenced_string                  ␛[0mA YARA string is never used in the condition, which
                                          libyara refuses unless the condition uses them.
␛[1myara_x_incompatible                       ␛[0mlibyara 4.5 compiles this YARA but YARA-X 1.x refuses it.
␛[1myara_x_only_syntax                        ␛[0mThis YARA uses syntax only YARA-X has, and the platform
                                          profile has yara_x_syntax refused: the platform may not
                                          accept it.
␛[1myaral_condition_shape                     ␛[0mThe condition is not one Google compiles: `not` or a comma
                                          on event terms, `or` across too many event variables or in
                                          an unbounded condition, or non-existence without a window
                                          and a bounded event.
␛[1myaral_deprecated_field                    ␛[0mThe UDM field is deprecated.
␛[1myaral_enum_value                          ␛[0mThe value is not one of the enumerated UDM field's values.
␛[1myaral_export_value                        ␛[0mAn `export` `write_row` value is not an outcome variable:
                                          Google exports outcome variables only.
␛[1myaral_function_unavailable                ␛[0mThe function exists, but not in this profile (rules or
                                          search).
␛[1myaral_leading_wildcard_regex              ␛[0mThe regular expression starts with `.*` without an anchor:
                                          RE2 matches anywhere already, and the prefix only costs
                                          time.
␛[1myaral_match_shape                         ␛[0mA YARA-L `match` is not a `YaraLMatch` object.
␛[1myaral_match_variable                      ␛[0mA `match` name is not a placeholder bound in `events`.
␛[1myaral_match_window                        ␛[0mA YARA-L `match` window is not a duration in `m`, `h` or
                                          `d`, or is longer than its kind allows.
␛[1myaral_meta_duplicate                      ␛[0mA meta key appears twice, or a meta value is not a
                                          double-quoted string.
␛[1myaral_multi_event_match                   ␛[0mA rule with two or more event variables has no `match`
                                          section.
␛[1myaral_nocase_on_enum                      ␛[0m`nocase` is applied to a comparison with an enumerated UDM
                                          field.
␛[1myaral_option                              ␛[0mA YARA-L `options` key is unknown, or its value is of the
                                          wrong kind.
␛[1myaral_outcome_aggregation                 ␛[0mWith `match`, an outcome reads an event field, or a
                                          placeholder that is not a `match` variable, outside an
                                          aggregation; or it aggregates an outcome variable.
␛[1myaral_outcome_limit                       ␛[0mA rule or search assigns more than 20 outcome variables.
␛[1myaral_parse_error                         ␛[0mThe YARA-L text does not parse, or a text holds a second
                                          rule.
␛[1myaral_reference_list_deprecated           ␛[0mReference lists are deprecated from May 2027 and migrate
                                          to data tables by July 2027: use a data table
                                          (`%table.column`).
␛[1myaral_reference_list_limit                ␛[0mMore `in` statements than the profile allows (rules: 10, 5
                                          with regex, 5 with cidr; search: 7, 4, 2).
␛[1myaral_regex                               ␛[0mThe regular expression is not valid RE2.
␛[1myaral_reserved_identifier                 ␛[0mA YARA-L keyword is used as a rule name, meta key or
                                          variable, or a variable is named `$window_start` or
                                          `$window_end`.
␛[1myaral_section_alias                       ␛[0mA YARA-L section key is a YAML alias instead of its own
                                          text.
␛[1myaral_section_empty                       ␛[0mA YARA-L section key is present with no text.
␛[1myaral_section_header                      ␛[0mA YARA-L section text holds a section label, a `rule`
                                          header or a rule's braces.
␛[1myaral_section_missing                     ␛[0mA YARA-L rule has no `events` or no `condition` section.
␛[1myaral_section_order                       ␛[0mA YARA-L section is repeated or out of order (meta, setup,
                                          events, match, outcome, condition, options, export).
␛[1myaral_section_unavailable                 ␛[0mThe section is not part of this profile: `dedup`, `order`,
                                          `limit`, `select` and `unselect` are search sections;
                                          `meta`, `setup` and `options` are rule sections.
␛[1myaral_string_escape                       ␛[0mA double-quoted string holds an escape Google does not
                                          document (only backslash, double quote, n, r and t); the
                                          tenant decides whether it compiles.
␛[1myaral_type                                ␛[0mAn operator or function is applied to a value of the wrong
                                          type: a count compared with a string, `any` or `all` on a
                                          map key, `nocase` on a number.
␛[1myaral_undefined_variable                  ␛[0mA variable in `match`, `outcome` or `condition` is not
                                          defined by `events` or `outcome`, or an event variable of
                                          `events` is absent from `condition`.
␛[1myaral_unfiltered_event                    ␛[0mAn event variable has no equality on
                                          `metadata.event_type`, `metadata.log_type` or
                                          `metadata.product_name`, so the rule scans every event.
␛[1myaral_unknown_function                    ␛[0mThe function is not in Google's YARA-L function list, or
                                          it takes a different number of arguments.
␛[1myaral_unknown_udm_field                   ␛[0mThe field path is not in the Unified Data Model.
␛[1myaral_window_bound                        ␛[0m`window_start` or `window_end` is used in `events`, or in
